BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Artist Talk: Enzo Camacho and Ami Lien
DTSTART:20261104T000000
DTEND:20261104T000000
DTSTAMP:20261031T163846Z
UID:bb5eb851a4c975ffce91a0c4dd0002@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Join visual artists and Harvard alumni Enzo Camacho (A.B. ’0
 7) and Ami Lien (A.B. ’09) as they share insights and developments into 
 their practice as artistic collaborators. Working between New York\, Berli
 n\, and Manila\, Camacho and Lien develop research-based\, site-specific\,
  and documentary projects to examine histories of labor\, land\, and resis
 tance in the Philippines. Their research on the enduring influence of Alfo
 nso Ossorio’s mural commission at the Chapel of St. Joseph the Worker on
  Negros Island has led them to investigate the sugar plantation landscape 
 that grounds this historic site-specific artwork. In their ongoing engagem
 ent with Negros Island\, the artists focus on the defiant forms of culture
 -making that emerge out of and in opposition to plantation violence. This 
 program is offered in conjunction with Alfonso Ossorio: Line and Lineage (
 October 23\, 2026–April 11\, 2027) in Gallery 1120 at the Harvard Art Mu
 seums and Knowledge Is Myth: Chimeric Continuities (October 1–December 1
 3\, 2026) at the Carpenter Center for Visual Arts. LEARN MORE / GET TICKET
 S Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/artist
 -talk%3a-enzo-camacho-and-ami-lien/93974/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 mil
 es of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusett
 s-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/artist-talk%3a
 -enzo-camacho-and-ami-lien/93974/
LOCATION:Harvard Art Museums\, Harvard Art Museums 32 Quincy Street\, Camb
 ridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/artist-talk%3a-enzo-camacho-and-ami-l
 ien/93974/
END:VEVENT
