BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Natanya
DTSTART:20261105T000000
DTEND:20261105T000000
DTSTAMP:20261031T163846Z
UID:f579379d9f31ac3e0b9d5d8de9cfd0@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:London-based singer-songwriter and producer Natanya is emergin
 g as one of pop’s most compelling new voices\, crafting music that blend
 s emotional candor with sharp\, self-assured production. Raised in North W
 est London\, she began playing classical piano at just four years old and 
 quickly discovered her perfect pitch\, later refining her musicianship at 
 the Julian Joseph Jazz Academy. Early influences spanning Janet Jackson\, 
 Amy Winehouse\, Paramore\, and Stevie Wonder helped shape her genre-fluid 
 sensibility. While studying English literature at University College Londo
 n\, Natanya wrote and produced her debut project\, Sorrow at Sunrise (2023
 )\, a coming-of-age tape structured as a series of diaristic reflections. 
 She expanded her sonic world with the dual EP releases Feline’s Return (
 with lead singles "Daydream\," "Dangerous\," and "Guitar")\, and Feline’
 s Return Act II (with lead singles "Jezebel\," "Meeting You Once (the End)
 \," "On Ur Time\," and "Sofa Joy\," all of which gained significant moment
 um. These recordings marked a confident shift toward a more polished\, pop
 -forward sound that retained her introspective edge. Natanya’s music has
  received early yet abundant critical acclaim. She won Guap Gala's Music A
 rtist to Watch award in 2023\, an honor previously given to the girl group
  FLO. Natanya also been featured in many magazines\, including Paper\, Pit
 chfork\, Clash\, NME\, and Dazed. Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https:/
 /www.meetboston.com/event/natanya/90934/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 mile
 s of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts
 -events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/natanya/90934/
LOCATION:The Red Room at Cafe 939\, 939 Boylston St\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/natanya/90934/
END:VEVENT
